[BLAME] benchmark_3/parts/semver_solver/lib/semver_solver_impl.py: The latest change adds defensive guards that remain unreachable under the specification contract. These statements can never execute: the continuation taken when two numeric prerelease identifiers compare equal as integers, and the trailing zero return of the same precedence routine, because identical prerelease tuples are already resolved before segment iteration and the required version grammar forbids numerically equal yet textually distinct numeric identifiers; the operator fall-through in comparator expansion, because every relational and prefix operator the range syntax recognizes is explicitly handled; the duplicate wildcard-position guard, because the preceding scan guarantees every component before the first wildcard component is non-wildcard; and the empty-accumulation guard at the end of clause parsing, because empty clauses are rejected by clause tokenization and every comparator expansion yields at least one comparator. Restructure each of these statements out of the implementation, or annotate it with '# pragma: no cover (assumption: <reason>)' as an impossible branch guaranteed by the contract.
